      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Heat the oven to 200°C. Toss the potato slices with 2 tablespoons of olive oil, the garlic, rosemary sprigs, and a generous grind of black pepper. Spread in a single layer on a large baking tray. Roast for 20 minutes until beginning to turn golden at the edges."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Remove the tray from the oven. Pour the white wine over the potatoes and add the lemon slices, tucking them in among the potato. Stir briefly."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Lay the sea bass fillets skin-side up over the potatoes. Drizzle with the remaining 2 tablespoons of olive oil. Return to the oven and roast for 12 to 15 minutes until the fish skin is golden and the flesh flakes easily."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Check the fish is cooked through by pressing the thickest part . it should feel firm rather than soft and the flesh should be opaque."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Squeeze the juice of the second lemon over the fish. Scatter with chopped parsley and serve directly from the tray."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Fish overcooked and dry",
              "solution": "Sea bass cooks faster than you expect. Check it from 10 minutes. The fish is done the moment it flakes easily - any more time dries it out."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Potatoes still firm when fish is ready",
              "solution": "The potato slices were too thick or the first roasting phase too short. Aim for 3mm slices and make sure they are golden before adding the fish."
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "problem": "Fish skin not crispy",
              "solution": "Pat the skin very dry before putting it on the tray and make sure the tray is hot when you add the fish. The skin side should face up in this recipe to crisp in the oven heat."
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Sea bass is caught along almost every stretch of the Italian coast. This style of baking it over potatoes is found from Liguria in the north to Sicily in the south. Each cook adds their own herbs and wine. It is the sort of dish that Italian families make without a recipe. The ingredients are simple and the method is easy to remember."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
